      "writtenOn": "2024-02-20T19:18:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of adding two vendorhooks to the same function, can we consolidate these a bit?\n\nAssuming it has no side effects, you might first check the vtime_accounting_enabled_this_cpu(), and then call trace_android_vh_account_task_time() which can also return ticks ?\n\nIs there some reason I\u0027m missing why two of these hooks are needed?",
      "revId": "d2c2d90c7a128456f01b7a8c9d6fbcd6be89372e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e7b45f9e_a73ab825",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/cputime.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 514,
      "author": {
        "id": 1866058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-21T02:42:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think of your suggestions carefully but it looks like not easy to consolidate the two venderhooks. There are some logics after the first hook to return from this function. The first hook is used to change the logic after calling account_process_tick. The second hook is used to get the load statistics that are called by many of our internal drivers.",
      "parentUuid": "a86a4304_29771cf2",
      "revId": "d2c2d90c7a128456f01b7a8c9d6fbcd6be89372e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "265c58e7_4e760b2b",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/cputime.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 514,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-29T03:50:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These are side-effects of your internal logic. Can you not have one vendor hook that calls out to the separate hook logic on the vendor side?\n\nI recognize there is some pain with reworking existing vendorhook infrastructure, but also carrying multiple hooks in the same function is a little excessive (older kernels we sometimes add second hooks if the original hook was not sufficient, as we have to preserve KABI, but that\u0027s not the case for a new kernel).\n\n@tkjos@google.com: Your thoughts here?",
      "parentUuid": "e7b45f9e_a73ab825",
      "revId": "d2c2d90c7a128456f01b7a8c9d6fbcd6be89372e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "65956b68_30253a53",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/cputime.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 514,
      "author": {
        "id": 1866058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-05T09:26:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi John,We thought about it carefully, but it still wasn\u0027t easy to merge.\nvoid android_vh_account_process_tick_gran_handler(void *unused, int user_tick, int *ticks)\nThis will operate ticks, and then the subsequent hook can be called only when ticks is not 0. It is difficult to guarantee this logical relationship after merging.",
      "parentUuid": "265c58e7_4e760b2b",
      "revId": "d2c2d90c7a128456f01b7a8c9d6fbcd6be89372e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1978f725_070d5571",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/cputime.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 514,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-06T19:24:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These could be combined since vtime_accounting_enabled_this_cpu() doesn\u0027t change any state and the 2nd hook can do the same calculation that the first one did to see if tick\u003d\u003d0. So this could reduce to:\n```\n\ttrace_android_vh_account_task_time(p, this_rq(), user_tick, \u0026ticks);\n\tif (!ticks)\n\t\treturn;\n\n\tif (vtime_accounting_enabled_this_cpu())\n\t\treturn;\n```\nYou could also move the `if (vtime_accounting...)` test above the hook (or call it from within the hook).",
      "parentUuid": "65956b68_30253a53",
      "revId": "d2c2d90c7a128456f01b7a8c9d6fbcd6be89372e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
